module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.helper_rematching_a_plan_its_caller_already_discriminated

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data helper_rematching_a_plan_its_caller_already_discriminated: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "helper_rematching_a_plan_its_caller_already_discriminated" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a helper receives the inputs of a decision its caller has already made, and makes the decision AGAIN -- re-calling the discriminator and handling only the interesting arm. The arms it declines to handle have to return SOMETHING, and what they return is almost always the empty value of the helper's own result type: [] for a list, \"\" for a script, none for an optional. That empty value is indistinguishable, at every site downstream, from a legitimate 'there was nothing to do'. The caller's discrimination is therefore not only duplicated, it is defeatable one layer down: a REFUSED input reaches the helper and comes back looking like a successful no-op.",

    "HARM: a fail-open that reads as convergence. The refused case produces no artifact and no complaint, so the composed plan is shorter rather than wrong-shaped, and the only witness that could notice is one that asserts the artifact EXISTS -- a claim written as 'the emitted script contains X' passes over an empty script only if X is absent from the comparison too, which is exactly what happens when the witness obtains both sides from the same re-matching helper. SPECIMEN (gunbc.live_deploy.emit / gunbc.host.host_axis_caps, landed by W8/PB2 after the census in the shell-to-dag residual program): apply_slice_control_converge_steps(spec) re-called slice_control_plan_for(host) and returned [] on SliceControlPlanNotOwed AND SliceControlPlanRefused, while its sibling apply_slice_control_converge_fragments poisoned Refused; one layer below, slice_control_converge_stmts(host) did the same, and its [] becomes an EMPTY SCRIPT via shell_command_text_of_stmts.",

    "WHY THAT IS LATENT RATHER THAN LIVE, STATED SO THE NEXT READER DOES NOT OVER- or UNDER-WEIGH IT: the only production caller matched the plan itself and passed the Derived case down, so the Refused arm was never entered on the apply route. The hole was reachable by TYPE, not by CALL. That distinction is the whole point of the row -- a latent fail-open is not fixed by the sibling that poisons, because the sibling protects only the route it is on. The same defect class becomes live the first time a second caller appears on the unprotected route, and helper functions attract second callers.",

    "FIX, BY CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN BY GUARD: change the parameter so the unhandled arms cannot be expressed. apply_slice_control_converge_steps and slice_control_converge_stmts / deploy_slice_control_converge_script now take units: FreeSemigroup<SliceControlUnit> -- the payload of the SliceControlPlanDerived arm, on the canonical non-empty carrier -- instead of a DeploymentSpec or a HostIdentity, so a Refused or NotOwed plan has no representation at the call site and no arm is needed to refuse it. A guard (`=> refuse(...)` added inside the re-match) was NOT used: it leaves the duplicate discriminator in place, and the next edit that touches the arms can re-open the hole while still type-checking. Discriminate once, in the caller, and pass the already-discriminated payload down.",

    "EXECUTED, NOT READ: the discrimination was performed twice on the same value in the same call chain (fragments matched it, then the helper re-derived it for the same host), and the second copy's unhandled arms were reachable by the type while being unreachable by the program -- verified by enumerating callers of apply_slice_control_converge_steps / deploy_slice_control_converge_script / slice_control_converge_stmts rather than by reading one call site. THE EXISTING WITNESS DID NOT HAVE THIS HOLE, AND SAYING SO IS WHAT KEEPS THE ROW CREDIBLE: witness_apply_script_converges_sessions_and_broker_slice_control obtained BOTH sides of its equality from the re-matching helpers (script from deploy_slice_control_converge_script(host), steps from apply_slice_control_converge_steps(spec)), so a Refused plan WOULD have compared \"\" to \"\" -- but the witness first composed the fragments itself and returned false on HostScriptRefused, and it required sessions.slice, gunbc-approval-broker.slice and the cap byte values, so a route that emitted nothing could not have passed it. The fail-open was therefore in the HELPERS, which no production caller reached with a Refused plan and no witness exercised: latent by type, not live by call, and not a witness defect. W8 removes those branches structurally by making the helper take the Derived units as its parameter, so the refused arms have no expression site left and a future second caller cannot reach them.",

    "THE EMPTY ROSTER IS NOW UNWRITABLE, NOT REFUSED: the roster (SliceControlPlanDerived, and the SliceControl caps it is derived from) is a std.algebra::FreeSemigroup, whose head: T makes a zero-unit plan impossible to construct -- the empty case is a TYPE ERROR, not a branch. That replaces the earlier receipt, which recorded an empty-roster refusal arm as deferred debt on the grounds that the empty plan was unreachable anyway; ruling nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved and DESIGN §3b (Cardinality/absence) say the carrier should have been non-empty from the start, and DESIGN §5 is explicit that a dissolution condition describes how admitted debt ends but does not authorize creating it. So no units == [] arm exists and none is needed: the law lives in the type, not in a guard. THE LAW STAYS WHERE IT WAS: A HOST WITH NO DERIVABLE UNIT ROSTER EMITS A REFUSAL, NOT AN EMPTY SCRIPT. An empty script applies cleanly and reports nothing, which is the quietest possible way to not converge a host.",

    "RELATED, DISTINCT: a helper that returns [] where its sibling poisons is the same defect with the arms visible in one file (the fragments/steps pair above); this row is about the arms being invisible because they live in a re-derivation in a different module. Distinct also from fold_accumulator_typed_from_init_not_from_the_expected_type (a type-inference gap that refuses loudly) -- this one never refuses at all, which is why it needs a row: nothing in the compiler will ever catch it.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, latent -- a silent default reachable by type and not yet by call, so it cost nothing here and would cost the whole route the first time it is reached. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed: a helper's parameter admits only the already-discriminated payload of one arm, so an unhandled arm cannot be passed to it. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, AT CAPABILITY GRAIN AND NAMING NOTHING THAT DOES NOT EXIST: a call-site narrowing judgment -- one that checks, when a helper is handed the payload of ONE arm of a named sum, that the caller actually narrowed to that arm, instead of trusting the parameter name to imply it. NO SUCH CAPABILITY EXISTS TODAY, which is exactly why the rung is 1 and not 3: today the narrowing is established by the helper taking the arm payload as its parameter plus a reviewer reading the one call site, and nothing in the language prevents a second caller from re-discriminating the same value. If that judgment ever lands, the CEILING above stops being reviewer-enforced and this row should be re-read. Until then the discipline is textual: a `let x = <discriminator>(..)` followed downstream by a second call to the same discriminator is the shape to reject. Deliberately not given a dotted capability id -- §3 treats a citation whose home does not resolve as a defect, and §3 (v1_seed_standing) freezes v1 semantics, so a new language judgment could not live there even once it exists.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a helper that calls a discriminator (something returning a sum whose arms the caller must handle) and whose body has an arm returning [] / \"\" / none / an identity value while a DIFFERENT function on the same input poisons or refuses that arm. Do not repair by adding a refusal arm inside the duplicate match -- narrow the parameter to the discriminated payload and delete the duplicate.",
    "2026-10-30: slice_control_converge_stmts and deploy_slice_control_converge_script are deleted with the instance apply's slice-control family, which had no executing consumer left. The FreeSemigroup<SliceControlUnit> parameter survives where the slice control still runs, gunbc.host.host_effect_realize dark_slice_control_legs.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
